  "notesHtml": "<ol>\n          <li>(a) Membership fees collected in cash are deferred, not earned immediately &#x2014; the whole $11,600 is a liability increase (Deferred Revenue), with no income statement effect yet.</li>\n          <li>(b) COGS reduces the Merchandise Inventory asset and is recognized as an expense, which flows through Earned Capital and Net Income.</li>\n          <li>(c) Use the inventory roll-forward: Beginning Inventory + Purchases &#x2212; COGS = Ending Inventory, so Purchases = Ending &#x2212; Beginning + COGS = $38,900 &#x2212; $34,200 + $410,500 = $415,200. Purchasing on account has no income statement effect &#x2014; it's a pure balance sheet swap (inventory up, payables up).</li>\n        </ol>"
